{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791626411,"nonce":"479RLFkdWX5zL6fefN1HDJFMykc=","title":"More pipeline passes allocate or recompute what they only read","message":"After 343befa, sampling the static-hot pipeline (method_call, tokenize, records start-ups, Mac) still showed: drop_insert's use index collecting each instruction's operands into a Vec (Users::of, derived_values_using); the inliner recomputing every callee's shape on each of its inner iterations and cloning an extern's link name on every call it classifies; cse's same_constants cloning and hashing each constant's HirType; phi_prune keeping its own edge rebuild, building a predecessor set for every block whether or not it has phis, and collapsing phis through a SipHash map; HirFunction::sweep_unreferenced_values growing its set from empty.\n\nFix: for_each_operand/any_operand in drop_insert; callee shapes kept across the inliner's iterations for callees not being optimised, and is_real_call reads the link name in place; same_constants keyed by CseCtx::type_id; phi_prune uses HirFunction::rebuild_cfg_edges (which also counts pattern-match edges its copy missed), checks stale incomings only where a block has phis, against its predecessor list, and collapses through an IdMap; the sweep's set is sized to the value table.\n\nStart-up instructions over 31e08890 (llvm-backend build, PROFILE_STARTUP=10, Mac): Lua 17 benchmarks, median of 3, 22.51G -\u003e 22.39G (-0.5%); with 7 runs method_call -3.0%, nbody -2.1%, lambda_call and free_function_call flat. method_call's count is bimodal run to run (3.9G or 4.65G with the same binary). Optimised bodies identical after id masking on all 17 Lua benchmarks and 6 Python kernels (ZYNTAX_DISABLE_WARM_UP=1).","files":null}]}